{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfla5ogbhw","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"SWE-Bench-CL harness uses eval_v1 not the Makefile, FAISS memory is a 3 method swap seam","summary":"Recon of agents-never-forget (commit 74a38a9). For a GRADED CL pilot use eval_v1/eval_procedure.py — it is the only version with real SWE-bench Docker grading (shells `python -m swebench.harness.run_evaluation` per task, dataset princeton-nlp/SWE-bench split test). eval_v2_agent has the nicer LangGraph agent but NO Docker grading (agent self-reports tests_passed) and its SWEBenchCLEvaluator is a broken stub. The Makefile + scripts/*.py eval targets are DEAD (reference nonexistent files + a root SWE-Bench-CL.json that doesn't exist; real data is data/SWE-Bench-CL-Curriculum.json). eval_v1 is a jupytext notebook-as-script (no __main__, runs top-to-bottom). FAISS memory seam = one duck-typed MemorySystem class with exactly 3 methods: get_relevant_context_for_prompt(problem, seq_id, k)->str (retrieve, returns prompt block), add_experience_to_memory(task_id, seq_id, problem, patch, harness_bool) (write verified outcome), clear_memory(). Toggle already exists (EXPERIMENT_CONDITIONS memory_enabled/disabled => OFF vs FAISS); 3rd Zonoid arm = a ZonoidMemorySystem hitting daemon HTTP /search (ungated) + /record_decision, selected by a one-line MEMORY_BACKEND branch at the constructor. Pilot sequence pick: pytest-dev_pytest_sequence (19 tasks, 8/8/3 easy/med/hard, 37% have CL dependencies). Top unknown: confirm daemon /search + /record_decision accept a workspace/namespace param over plain HTTP for arm isolation (FAISS clear_memory has no Zonoid equivalent). Deps are UNPINNED (requirements.txt is dataset-construction only) — langchain/faiss-cpu/swebench must be pinned; dependency rot is the main risk.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T19:11:29.344Z","vec":[-0.05909937620162964,0.03704388439655304,-0.08072523027658463,0.015441810712218285,0.021029923111200333,-0.0810322389